{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "Review value/attention-worthiness — which reviews merit attention based on their sentiment signal and community-perceived helpfulness/engagement",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "review_length",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "A generic textual metric, but plausibly a proxy for review substance/detail that feeds an attention-worthiness framing; weakly supportive rather than central."
    },
    {
      "name": "sentiment",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Categorical sentiment identifies the valence of feedback, directly relevant to 'what's worth attention' (e.g., surfacing negatives)."
    },
    {
      "name": "helpfulness_ratio",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Normalizes the existing helpfulness numerator/denominator into a community-perceived usefulness signal — a strong facet of which reviews are worth attention."
    },
    {
      "name": "has_criticism",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Flags actionable negative content, directly aligned with 'actionable' reviews to investigate."
    },
    {
      "name": "engagement_level",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Buckets attention/engagement, a coherent facet of prioritizing reviews worth attention."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.62,
  "structure_quality": 0.55,
  "focus_actionability": 0.6,
  "rationale": "The columns loosely orbit a single inferable focus — the attention-worthiness/value of a review — via helpfulness, sentiment, criticism, and engagement. However coherence is diluted: sentiment and has_criticism are largely redundant (both encode negative valence), and review_length is a bare mechanical text metric that does not cleanly join the focus. The set mixes an actionable value/prioritization theme (helpfulness_ratio, has_criticism, engagement_level) with generic NLP features (length, bare sentiment), so it is neither a tight facet decomposition nor pure noise. The implied focus is genuinely actionable — an analyst could triage low-helpfulness or critical reviews — but the framing is only partially realized because no column resolves what the reviews are actually ABOUT (topics/product aspects), leaving the 'what's in these reviews' half of the query unaddressed. Solid but not tightly centred."
}

